/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/scripts/generate_mechanism_coalition_corpus.py:708:        f"**New trainable coalition-size histogram: {histogram}. Occupancy-activation is admitted by {summary['occupancy_activation_anchors_trainable']} of {summary['anchors']} anchors.**",
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/scripts/generate_mechanism_coalition_corpus.py:721:        f"- `occupancy-activation`: {summary['family_histogram_unique_rows'].get(OCCUPANCY_ACTIVATION, 0)} trainable rows across {summary['occupancy_activation_anchors_trainable']} anchors, by changed-user size {summary['family_size_histogram'].get(OCCUPANCY_ACTIVATION, {})}. Every seed beam starts at occupancy exactly 1 and two legal arrivals take it to occupancy 3. The exact activation core is retained as a pair; where a legal outside action exists, a three-change context probe adds a third changed user so the learner directly sees third-order variation around the same activation. The first activating occupancy is recomputed from `q10(elevation) * Gamma(n)` using the full Rician×shadow distribution and the engine tables at the weakest actual link elevation among incumbents and selected arrivals; the 10-degree authentication point is `q10 = 0.42923539` and the lowest threshold remains `0.7174947935658479`. Its exact-Psi sign/distribution ledger is {summary['family_psi_normalized_distributions'].get(OCCUPANCY_ACTIVATION, {})}.",
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/scripts/generate_mechanism_coalition_corpus.py:722:        f"- `occupancy-2-diminishing`: {summary['family_histogram_unique_rows'].get(OCCUPANCY_2_DIMINISHING, 0)} rows across {summary['occupancy_2_diminishing_anchors']} anchors, kept separate from occupancy activation. These start at occupancy 2 and add two users, so the first arrival crosses occupancy 3 and the second exposes the corrected diminishing population. Its exact-Psi sign/distribution ledger is {summary['family_psi_normalized_distributions'].get(OCCUPANCY_2_DIMINISHING, {})}.",
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-curve-ws/scripts/generate_mechanism_coalition_corpus.py:724:        f"- `beam-evacuation`: {summary['family_histogram_unique_rows'].get(BEAM_EVACUATION, 0)} rows. Every beam with 2 or 3 occupants is evacuated when every occupant has a different legal alternative. This selection uses occupancy and legal-action identity only; it consults no decode threshold.",
